prompt Kyri: keep taking the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Season A road; approve your own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates.
think HUNK35 (preset_detail) landed and sent; its first named horizon was the Skate view of the detail — a book shown as a shelf of named chips. Lindy-first crux-first: the library is read every time the Photos app opens, and it composes two proven seams (HUNK35's honest detailing + the Skate grid) rather than inventing a pipeline.
think Chose the home carefully. The DetailListing lives in pond/apps with its full verified-store chain; the Skate grid lives in brushstroke. pond/apps already carries a `brushstroke/` symlink, so `@import("brushstroke/skate_grid.rye")` resolves with zero new symlinks — the shelf's natural home is pond/apps.
think The property this rung earns: a view must never quietly hide a book. shelf_grid refuses ShelfTooSmall when the grid has fewer rows than books — the display-side echo of HUNK35's whole-detailing honesty. Upstream never advertises a phantom; downstream never omits a real one.
obs The shelf is a PURE view over an already-honest detailing, so it can add no new way to lie — proven by building twice for identical cells and fg_index with the detailing untouched. The book name wears a real palette slot (a chip) distinct from the presets beside it (put_color_run + put_line composed).
obs Witness GREEN on first run (72x4 shelf, 1607 lit pixels). tame_style_check bans clean; width-check exit 0 — the single usize is the sanctioned @as(usize,...) allocation seam cast, matching preset_preview's own idiom, none in authored API. No network, no key, no funds; no custody gate reached.
